+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm install`, then `pnpm start`. The default port is 11222; override it
+with the `PORT` environment variable.
+
+## Local network access
+
+The server sends a `Permissions-Policy` header allowing this application's
+origin to request local network and loopback resources. It includes the legacy
+`local-network-access` directive for older browsers. If deployed through a
+different static host, configure that host to send the same response header:
+
+```http
+Permissions-Policy: local-network=(self), loopback-network=(self), local-network-access=(self)
+```
+
+Serve the deployed app over HTTPS. The browser still asks the user for access
+when a local connection is attempted. If the app is embedded in a cross-origin
+iframe, its parent must also delegate `local-network` and `loopback-network`
+(or `local-network-access` on older browsers) through its iframe `allow`
+attribute and any applicable parent Permissions-Policy.
+
+When adding device requests, initiate the first connection from a user action
+and declare the target address space for HTTP endpoints:
+
+```js
+// Run from a user-initiated connection handler, using the user's service URL.
+const response = await fetch(serviceUrl, {
+  targetAddressSpace: 'local', // Use 'loopback' for localhost / 127.0.0.1 / ::1.
+});
+if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Service returned HTTP ${response.status}`);
+```
+
+The local service must allow the app's origin through CORS. This header does
+not grant user consent, override an embedding page's policy, or bypass CORS.
+There are no device URLs configured and no network probes on page load.
+
+See [Chrome's local network access guidance](https://github.com/GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance/blob/main/skills/modern-web-guidance/guides/security/local-network-access.md).
